<article class="env-lemma" id="0F2D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F2D">Lemma <span data-tag="0F2D">52.27.1</span>.</a> Let $(A, \mathfrak m)$ be a Noetherian local ring and $f \in \mathfrak m$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$A$ is $f$-adically complete, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ is a nonzerodivisor, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$H^1_\mathfrak m(A/fA)$ and $H^2_\mathfrak m(A/fA)$ are finite $A$-modules, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$H^3_\mathfrak m(A/fA) = 0$<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001120346" id="a0001120346-mark"><sup>1</sup></a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Let $U$, resp. $U_0$ be the punctured spectrum of $A$, resp. $A/fA$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _{U_0 \subset U' \subset U\text{ open}} \mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}\nolimits (U') \longrightarrow \mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}\nolimits (U_0)  \]
</div>
  <p> is surjective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $U_0 \subset U_ n \subset U$ be the $n$th infinitesimal neighbourhood of $U_0$. Observe that the ideal sheaf of $U_ n$ in $U_{n + 1}$ is isomorphic to $\mathcal{O}_{U_0}$ as $U_0 \subset U$ is the principal closed subscheme cut out by the nonzerodivisor $f$. Hence we have an exact sequence of abelian groups 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}\nolimits (U_{n + 1}) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}\nolimits (U_ n) \to H^2(U_0, \mathcal{O}_{U_0}) = H^3_\mathfrak m(A/fA) = 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       see More on Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0C6R" data-tag="0C6R">37.4.1</a>. Thus every invertible $\mathcal{O}_{U_0}$-module is the restriction of an invertible coherent formal module, i.e., an invertible object of $\textit{Coh}(U, f\mathcal{O}_ U)$. We conclude by applying Lemma <a href="/tag/0EKZ" data-tag="0EKZ">52.24.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>